    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40153" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quingēni</span></b> , ae, a, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>num. distr. adj.</i>
			[quingenti]. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Five hundred each</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quingenos denarios dat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 16, 8, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4, 16, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 101</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Caes. 38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Ner. 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 38,
				1, 15</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In gen., <i>five hundred</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 5, 2,
			6</span></i>.</div>
